src/app.module.ts is the NestJS root module. The layer model places it in the presentation layer through the **/*.module.ts pattern, so its job is to wire the app together, which NestJS module files are expected to do. Everything in the file is declarative wiring:
- it imports the feature and infrastructure modules;
- it registers ConfigModule;
- it passes connection settings and the ORM entity list to TypeOrmModule.forRoot;
- it applies ContextMiddleware to all routes in configure().

The file does not query or save data itself, contains no transport or request-handling code beyond registering middleware, and has no business rules or domain calculations. TypeOrmModule.forRoot is configuration for a persistence framework, not persistence code running in this file. Wiring like this is the expected job of a root module, so I don't count it as a responsibility from another layer. Some things could be improved but don't break the rule: the long hard-coded entity list (autoLoadEntities would avoid it) and synchronize: true. No ADR text was provided to contradict this reading.

